%% Figure 4. Dynamic view SD-2 (QAS-5): the API is asleep or restarting while a job seeker applies
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor S as Job Seeker
  participant W as Web App (Draft Store, API Client)
  participant R as Render free host
  participant T as Tamkeen API
  participant I as Idempotency Filter
  participant D as Main Database
  Note over S,D: Legend: solid arrow = request, dashed arrow = reply, X arrow = failed call, rect = retry loop
  S->>W: Presses "Send application"
  W->>W: Draft Store saves form + Idempotency-Key K
  W-xR: POST /v1/applications (K)
  Note over R,T: Service was idle more than 15 min, spin-up takes about 1 min
  W->>W: API Client timeout after 10 s (or 502/503)
  W-->>S: aria-live: "Connecting. Your answers are saved."
  R->>T: start instance
  rect rgb(235, 242, 250)
    loop every 2, 4, 8, 16, 30, 30 s (max 120 s)
      W->>R: GET /health
      R-->>W: 503 or no answer until the API is up
    end
  end
  R->>T: instance ready
  W->>T: GET /health
  T-->>W: 200 OK
  W->>I: POST /v1/applications again, same Idempotency-Key K
  alt K not seen (first POST never reached the API)
    I->>D: reserve K, then normal apply (see SD-1)
    I-->>W: 201 Created
  else K already completed (first POST was processed before the timeout)
    I->>D: read stored response for K
    I-->>W: 201 Created (replayed, no second application)
  end
  W->>W: Draft Store clears K
  W-->>S: aria-live: "Application sent"
  opt API still down after 120 s
    W-->>S: "We could not reach the server. Your application is saved on this device."
  end
